00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:11.900
Joseph Denman: It occurred to me that, yeah, over time, adding support for every data type that we would want that has some sort of addition operation is kind of infeasible.

49
00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:21.490
Joseph Denman: you define, you know, add operations for any number of types in different ways that you might want, so I was just wondering if this kind of abstraction in the wrong direction

50
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:28.329
Joseph Denman: And maybe what we wanted is something like, an add trait on structs or custom.

