00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:23.290
Kent Dybvig: But you should do that as a special case for the curve points.

98
00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:32.149
Kent Dybvig: I mean, if the curve point… since the curve point… since the mole has two different types of operands, you could just say, oh, if you… if you switch the operands, you just…

99
00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:35.180
Kent Dybvig: You know, just treat it as if it were the…

100
00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:37.959
Kent Dybvig: You know, they were in different… the other order.

101
00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:53.479
Kent Dybvig: So what's the hidden failure mode that you're concerned about with using plus and minus? How does that differ from using EC Mall and EC…

